# APDUs that are wrong. Header failures are errors; anything else decodes,
# keeps what was odd about it, and round-trips.

80 00 => error pdu-type 8
f0 => error pdu-type 15
00 => error truncated 2/1
00 05 01 => error truncated 4/3
08 05 01 00 => error truncated 5/4
10 => error truncated 2/1
20 02 => error truncated 3/2
40 0b 01 => error truncated 4/3
50 03 => error truncated 3/2
# Reserved flag bits, kept and written back.
01 05 01 0c => confirmed-request invoke 1 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified reserved-flags 1
1f 08 => unconfirmed-request service 8 reserved-flags 15
33 01 0c => complex-ack invoke 1 service 12 reserved-flags 3
7e 05 04 => abort invoke 5 reason 4 reserved-flags 14
# Octets after a fixed-length PDU, which a conforming sender never adds.
20 02 0f 00 00 => simple-ack invoke 2 service 15 trailing 0000
# A reserved max-APDU code, and the reserved bit of the limits octet.
00 09 01 0c => confirmed-request invoke 1 service 12 max-apdu reserved 9 segments unspecified
00 85 01 0c => confirmed-request invoke 1 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified reserved-limit-bit
# More-follows on an unsegmented request: contradictory, and kept.
04 05 01 0c => confirmed-request invoke 1 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified more
